"test":{"name":"attrition-rule-transport-load","kind":"rules","opponent":"Human","rounds":"4","check":"transportLoad","question":"What fits where. An APC (2 slots, carries Boots) takes two grunts (weight 1) or one supply unit (weight 2), never a tank (Treads) or a fighter. A grunt cannot board a transport ship on open water beside the shore, but can at the naval yard's dock. A loaded APC can itself board the ship at the dock (it takes its own weight, 3 of the ship's 4), and everything aboard goes where the ship goes.","rules":"standard"},
